":"The stock rose about 138% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $95.28 and pulling back 21% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jun 7, 2001 it closed at $99.33, its first close above the base high of $94.46. Volume that day was 4.8M shares, 0.83x the prior 10-day average of 5.7M. It didn't hold. By Jun 20, 2001 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $79.00.","lesson":"This is an example of a false breakout. Volume on the breakout day was light, and that tell was visible before the move fell apart. Cutting it early was a good read."}}